  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250 accuracy. Evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder, multiprofile as essential, weighted fusion over concat (0.7131 vs 0.6878 with resnet50), and imagenet_vit_l over resnet50 (0.7250 vs 0.7131). The one remaining untested variable in this best-performing family is aggregation: transformer vs avgpool. In RNA-only multiprofile, the difference was negligible (0.6530 vs 0.6501), but in the multimodal setting with a stronger image encoder, the interaction could shift. Config_037 (avgpool + weighted + imagenet_vit_l) isolates this single change from the current best. As the final experiment, this is the most informative test: if it matches or beats config_039, it reveals aggregation is not a bottleneck; if it falls short, it confirms transformer is the right choice and solidifies config_039 as the definitive best. No other untested configuration has a realistic chance of exceeding 0.7250 given the strong evidence against scgpt, pca_n2000, or concat fusion."
}

